## Status: clean-room rewrite complete (2026-10-16)

This repository **no longer contains any upstream-derived code**. Every source
file under `src/` has been rewritten from scratch by this project's
contributors as an original implementation of the same behavioral
specification. A file-by-file blob-hash comparison against the historical
upstream baseline (`8311c9a`) shows **zero byte-identical source files** in
the working tree and at HEAD.

## What the project is

**Bannerlord-Blore** (MCP name `blore`) — a Bannerlord MCP server exposing
39 `ba_*` tools for mod development: XML/decompiled-source/README indexing
with SQLite + FTS5, entity lookups with localization resolution, mod-source
C# indexing via Roslyn, project memory (FTS-backed, cross-session), path-
sandboxed file access, workspace scaffolding, Harmony/XSLT patch generators,
and a doctor/verify toolchain.

## Historical note (recorded for provenance transparency only)

The project's lineage traces back to an unofficial variant of
`BannerlordSage` (MIT, © 2026 Vortex, © 2026 hby7921) at upstream commit
`8311c9a`. That heritage supplied the *behavioral specification* — tool
names, output shapes, index schemas, CLI flags — which this project
deliberately preserves for user compatibility. The code implementing that
specification is entirely ours:

- Clean-room rewrite rule applied: implementers worked from exported
  signatures and observable behavior; no upstream file was copied, adapted,
  or mechanically transformed.
- During the rewrite, ~640 lines of unreachable dead code (a full-rebuild
  XML index path stranded after an early `return`) were removed; the
  incremental path is the only implementation.
- The walkFiles symlink blind spot (Vortex-style mod installs invisible to
  the doctor) was fixed in this project earlier and remains ours.
- The knowledge base (`knowledge/`, FTS-indexed) and the editor-preview
  integration are this project's own additions.

Because the rewrite is complete, **no attribution to the historical upstream
is required** by license, though this notice preserves the lineage record.

## Runtime dependencies

